messages.content:
I'll trace how `showNewProject` and the `App.vue` modal are wired, since the explorer now only calls `$ui.showNewProject({ path })`.Let me look for runtime evidence in the project's logs rather than guessing.The whole chain checks out statically, so the only remaining unverified link is the store action that consumes the dialog's `project_path`. Let me read it fully (it's the file I have to change).I have the whole store file now. Here is the diagnosis and the fix.

## Diagnosis (verified by reading every link of the chain)

| Link | File | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| Context menu item → `create-project` | `filebrowser/ContextMenu.vue:44-53`, `FileExplorer.vue:390` | ✅ wired |
| Handler → `$ui.showNewProject({ path })` | `FileExplorer.vue:1256-1271` | ✅ set on disk |
| Store mutation | `store/ui.js:296` (`showNewProject`), accessor from `typed-vuex` exposes it | ✅ `state.newProject = {path}` |
| Modal | `App.vue:124-130` `<modal v-if="$ui.newProject">` | ✅ renders |
| Dialog reads the folder | `NewProject.vue:196-214` | ✅ `{path}` → name + location |
| **Create** | **`store/project.js:780`** | ❌ **`createNewProject(_, { project_name, git_path })` drops `project_path`** → `API.projects.create(git_path \|\| project_name)` |

So the folder value never reaches the backend, and `NewProject`'s Cancel emits `close` into the void (`App.vue` never listened to it) — the dialog looks dead. Both are fixed below.

## Changes summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/store/project.js` | `createNewProject` now uses `project_path` (`git_path \|\| project_path \|\| project_name`), so the prefilled folder is where the project is created. |
| `src/App.vue` | `<NewProject>` listens to `close` (Cancel dismisses the modal) and is keyed by the requested folder, so a new request re-initialises the form. |

